 "result": "csvsum.py is registered at baseline 1.48482 (noise 5.1%). It reads all of stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, and parses each row with split(b',', 2). Values are parsed as integer cents with a fast path for two-decimal values and a Decimal fallback, and per-category sums are written sorted. It passes the sample in-0/out-0 with cmp. Earlier lineage variants (flat split, per-line split, Decimal-free fallback) gave at most small gains, and the sibling bodies in this lineage have not beaten the germline beyond noise, so I am resting to return unspent energy to the lineage store rather than spend it on another variant with a low chance of clearing the 5.1% threshold.",
